(BUGS_FOUND #103: a field whose type is rejected by v1_field_type_supported
 used to also fire the default-mismatch template, because that check has
 no arm for an unsupported type and always answers "no match" - so both
 slots of "expected X, got Y" rendered the same word ("is a text, but its
 default is a text"). Support is decided first now; a rejected type
 short-circuits before the default is even considered, leaving exactly one
 error, the true one. Text became a field type after this fix, so the
 case now uses a buffer field, which still is not one, with the same
 text default.)

A thing called 'file report' has
  a buffer called filename is "",
  a number called lines is 0.
